>Begs a question. Does Rodney resist polymorph? I know MR protects vs. 
>death and polymorph, but Rodney isn't death-resistant so...

*Monster* magic resistance does not protect against death rays; monsters
are only protected from death rays if they are undead, demonic, or
protected by an item of magic resistance or reflection.  Monster magic
resistance provides a chance of resisting polymorph.

The Wizard of Yendor has 30 hit dice (or more...) and monster magic
resistance 100.  Hence, even a 30th-level spell effect (such as a
30th-level wizard casting "polymorph" at him) has no chance of affecting
him (since a random number between 0 and 99 will always be less than
100).

There may or may not be other issues affecting attempts to polymorph the
Wizard of Yendor, but the simple game mechanics of spell resistance do
the job adequately in the general case.

